 34AR c  2001Kh17: a 47-MeV/nucleon {+34}Ar beam was produced via the projectile
 34AR2c  fragmentation of a 95-MeV/nucleon {+36}Ar primary beam impinging on a  
 34AR3c  {+12}C target at GANIL. The secondary target was CH{-2}. The elastic   
 34AR4c  and inelastic protons were detected using the MUST Si-Si(Li)-CsI       
 34AR5c  telescope and heavy nuclei were analyzed by the SPEC spectrometer.     
 34AR6c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and deformation          
 34AR7c  parameters from Coupled-Channel Born Approximation (CCBA) using the    
 34AR8c  ECIS code and TAMURA-DWBA analyses of the measured |s(|q). Also see    
 34AR9c  2000KhZX, 2001Bl17, 2003La13 for more discussions on the same data.    
